# Keyboard shortcuts (SC) — mandatory

**Non-negotiable:** every user-facing button or primary control must have a keyboard shortcut. No exceptions for “secondary” actions (Choose, Refresh, Log out, Back, etc.).

## Required on every button

1. **Visible SC in the label** using the `Label · Shortcut` pattern (e.g. `Cancel · Esc`, `Choose · ⌘O`, `Skip · 1`).
2. **Wire the key** in a `keydown` handler (use capture when overlays/editors might swallow keys).
3. **Do not ship** a button whose only activation is mouse click.

## Defaults

| Action | Shortcut |
| --- | --- |
| Confirm / Continue / Save / Send | **Enter** |
| Cancel / Close overlay | **Esc** |
| Back (wizard step) | **Backspace** when not typing in a field |
| Open / Choose folder (in dialogs) | **⌘O** / **Ctrl+O** (intercept while dialog is open) |
| Mutually exclusive create options | Digit or letter keys shown on each option (`· 1`, `· 2`, …) |

## Checklist before finishing UI work

- [ ] Every `<button>` in the changed surface shows an SC in its label
- [ ] Matching `keydown` (or form submit) actually runs that action
- [ ] While typing in inputs, only Enter/Esc (and explicitly allowed chords like ⌘O) fire; bare letter shortcuts do not type-steal unless intended
- [ ] No trailing `…` ellipsis on action button labels (use clear verbs)
- [ ] UI copy in **English**

If you add a button and leave it without an SC, the change is incomplete — fix it before moving on.
